Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Shiny seems to handle text with a diaeresis incorrect. (as input or output) Example: ë is an Î, ï is an Ô, in general all vowels with a diaeresis shows something different then intended. I've tried addingoptions(encoding="UTF-8") but no improvement.

I hope someone stumbled on the same issue.

Reproducible example which handles text as input.

server.r
library(shiny)
options(encoding = "utf8")

# Define server logic
shinyServer(function(input, output) {
  datasetInput <- reactive({
  input$char
  })
})

ui.r
library(shiny)
# Define UI
shinyUI(pageWithSidebar(
# Application title
headerPanel("Test input characters"),
sidebarPanel(
textInput("char", "Write character", "")
),
mainPanel()
))

