Long story short, I had to run a number of experiments on digitalocean to see what was the reason and finally I found it - RAM. I used the cheapest droplet with 512 MB and it was not enough looks like for R packages to be installed properly. See my question for details. So, as I already had some stuff installed on my droplet, I just resized it by adding more RAM. It was easy to do and I picked up 1 GB. After that, no more issues. Hope this will save you some time. You would want more RAM to run R any ways.

