One thing to note is that the documentation you are seeing are for Bootstrap 3. Shiny (as of v0.8) uses Bootstrap 2 (http://getbootstrap.com/2.3.2/base-css.html)

The code for Bootstrap 2 is more like this

<div class="input-append">
<input class="span2" id="appendedInputButton" type="text">
<button class="btn" type="button">Go!</button>
</div>

Shiny actionButtons have a few extra properties so that it will be "pickup" by Shiny and you can type actionButton in the R console to see what they are. It gives

function (inputId, label)
{
    tags$button(id = inputId, type = "button", class = "btn action-button",
        label)
}

So I suspect what's missing is the action-button and inputId! So you can modify the above to read

<div class="input-append">
<input class="span2" id="appendedInputButton" type="text">
<button class="btn action-button" type="button" id ="myButton">Go!</button>
</div>

Now you should be able to use input$myButton in server.R as per usual. You can update the textbox to be pickup by Shiny using a similar investigative method I have shown.

